  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Palestinian General Federation of Trade Unions (PGFTU) signed an agreement with the Private Sector Cluster headed by the Chairman of the Federation of Palestinian Chambers of Commerce, Industry and Agriculture (FPCCIA) to protect workers and support employment and enterprises for two months during the COVID-19 crisis.
PGFTU effectively engage in the development of the Emergency Response and Recovery Plan. 

PGFTU developed a position paper concerning the enhancement of social security and labour market governance that was presented during the national tripartite social dialogue conference (March 2021).

PGFTU announced the creation of a nation wide coalition with prominent civil society oragnizations to join efforts in their advocacy and lobbying initiatives for labour law reforms, and impact socio-economic policies.

PGFTU negotiated and agreed on a new minimum wage in Palestine, increasing it from ILS 1,450 to ILS 1,880. ILO provide technical assistane and advice to the Palestinian General Federation of Trade Unions (PGFTU) prior signing the tripartite 2 months agreement in March, between the Ministry of Labour, the General Federation of Trade Unions, and the Private Sector Cluster.
ILO provided technical support to PGFTU to:
- conduct an awareness-raising campaign on OSH issues to ensure workplace safety and that appropriate measures are applied in the workplace to prevent the spread of COVID-19.
- finalize the position paper to enhance social security and labor market governance in Palestine.
- build a national coalition with CSO (the coalition was formally announced in April).
- prepare and effectively engage in the national tripartite social dialogue conference in March, including its negotiation to adjust the minimum wage.

The ITCILO conducted a training course for 67 particpants for PGFTU on &quot;Building Union Strength in Palestine through Social Dialogue and Collective Bargaining&quot; (November 2020 &#x2013; March 2021).</narrative>
   </description>
